  <div slot="species-facts">
    <p><span>Category: </span>Reptile</p>
    <p><span>Scientific name: </span>Viviparous lizard</p>
    <p><span>Length: </span>typically 10&ndash;15cm</p>
    <p><span>Status: </span>Common</p>
  </div>
  <div slot="species-info">
    <p>
      They are often found in open, sunny areas like heaths, moorlands, and dry
      stone walls.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Viviparous</strong> means they give birth to live young, not eggs.
    </p>
  </div>
